<article class="env-lemma" id="09AA">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09AA">Lemma <span data-tag="09AA">61.25.3</span>.</a> Let $i : Z \to X$ be a closed immersion of schemes. Then </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$i_{pro\text{-}\acute{e}tale}^{-1}$ commutes with limits, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$i_{{pro\text{-}\acute{e}tale}, *}$ is fully faithful, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$i_{pro\text{-}\acute{e}tale}^{-1}i_{{pro\text{-}\acute{e}tale}, *} \cong \text{id}_{\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (Z_{pro\text{-}\acute{e}tale})}$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Assertions (2) and (3) are equivalent by Sites, Lemma <a href="/tag/04D6" data-tag="04D6">7.41.1</a>. Parts (1) and (3) are (Zariski) local on $X$, hence we may assume that $X$ is affine. In this case the result follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/09BL" data-tag="09BL">61.25.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>